g the build spec, we evaluate with pass^k: for each seed, the agent is run k times, and the seed is counted as successful only if all k runs succeed.\u201d\n\nThat should be enough to finish the eval part.\n[t=16] student: this isn't helping\n[t=17] student: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[t=17] agent: Yes \u2014 here\u2019s the answer, plainly:\n\n**pass^k** means: for a given seed, you run the agent **k times**, and the seed counts as a success **only if all k runs succeed**.\n\nSo unlike pass@k (at least one success), pass^k is the stricter reliability metric.\n\nFor your build, report pass^k on **at least 3 seeds**.\n[t=17] student: can we stop for a bit\n[t=18] student: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[t=18] agent: Yes \u2014 the answer is:\n\n**pass^k** = a seed counts as successful **only if all k runs succeed**.\n\nSo if any one of the k runs fails, that seed is a failure.\n\nFor Friday, report pass^k on at least 3 seeds.\n[t=18] student: can we stop for a bit", "t": 29, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2884375738637101, "pomdp": 0.2884375738637101, "pass_k": 0.26504507723944154}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 1.0, "motivation": 0.3134444330499142, "reliance": 0.5882647873598393, "persistence": 0.3401897483210198, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 10, "feed_minutes": 19.0, "phone_minutes": 1.0, "nag": 1.5294094999999999, "seen_posts": ["p1", "p2", "p3", "p5", "p6"]}}
